text:
maria: Quick check — I'm about to open a PR that changes streaming for /v1/chat/completions when a model issues a function call. Proposal: emit a start/delta/end event sequence instead of only a final function_call at the end. Thoughts?

alex: Currently we only emit function_call at the final chunk. Partial args mid-stream would be a new shape for many SDKs. We need a clear event name and fallback for old clients.

ryan: Main worry is backward compatibility. Some clients assume function_call only shows up as a single final message (no streaming). If we stream parts, we should keep an unambiguous terminal event so older clients can ignore deltas and still get the full args.

maria: Proposed event sequence: `func_call.start` (name only), zero-or-more `func_call.arg_delta` (string chunks), `func_call.end` (complete arguments string). That way naive clients see nothing until `func_call.end`, and advanced clients can reassemble.

sam: That sounds OK. A couple of nitpicks: 1) ensure `func_call.arg_delta` uses UTF-8-safe chunking (no assumption about splitting inside codepoints). 2) define max chunk size and ordering token so reassembly is deterministic.

alex: Also, JSON vs raw string: should arg deltas be streamed as escaped JSON fragments or as plain text chunks? If we stream escaped fragments clients must concatenate and JSON-parse at the end. If we stream raw bytes we'd need `content-type` hint. My leaning: stream escaped JSON fragments as `delta` strings to match existing `content.delta` behavior.

maria: Agree on escaped JSON fragments — keeps parity with text deltas. We'll document that `func_call.end` contains the fully concatenated and parseable JSON string.

ryan: Edgecases: what if model aborts mid-arg and falls back to non-func output? We should include a `func_call.cancel` event or have `func_call.end` include `status: "cancelled"` metadata.

maria: Good call. Plan: `func_call.start` -> optional arg deltas -> `func_call.end` with {"status":"ok","arguments": "..."} or {"status":"cancelled"}. Older clients ignore deltas and consume `func_call.end` like before.

infra-bot: deploy-checklist: add feature gate `streaming_funccall_v2` (opt-in per-model) + docs + examples + integration tests.

sam: I'll add a short example to docs. Example client pseudocode:```js
let name = null
let argsBuf = ''
for await (const ev of stream) {
  if (ev.type === 'func_call.start') name = ev.name
  if (ev.type === 'func_call.arg_delta') argsBuf += ev.delta
  if (ev.type === 'func_call.end') {
    if (ev.status === 'ok') {
      const args = JSON.parse(argsBuf)
      callTool(name, args)
    } else {
      // fallback
    }
  }
}
```

alex: Tests: include clients that ignore `func_call.arg_delta` and still succeed by relying only on `func_call.end`. Also test partial chunk boundaries (split across multibyte chars).

ryan: LGTM from infra/compat perspective. Add an integration harness hitting the hosted API with the feature gate toggled.

maria: Thanks. I'll open the PR with the schema change, opt-in gate, and a short migration note. Ping me for review @alex @ryan @sam. :thumbsup:
